WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.387 --> 00:00:01.220
- Gasps!

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:04.264
- There's nothing in the human
world that feels like this.

00:00:04.264 --> 00:00:05.656
- Oh they are squishy.

00:00:05.656 --> 00:00:07.463
- What am I doing.

00:00:07.463 --> 00:00:08.436
- Smash it.

00:00:08.436 --> 00:00:09.269
- Squish squish.

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:10.102
- Squeeshy.

00:00:10.102 --> 00:00:12.234
- Squish squish bish.

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:15.712
(light playful music)

00:00:15.712 --> 00:00:17.457
- I have never heard of Squishies before.

00:00:17.457 --> 00:00:20.416
- Maybe they're a new
type of fidget spinner.

00:00:20.416 --> 00:00:24.353
- Squishies are these
little foamy creatures

00:00:24.353 --> 00:00:27.891
- I've seen other people with
them and I get super jealous

00:00:27.891 --> 00:00:31.418
and I really want one, it
look so fun and cool and cute.

00:00:31.418 --> 00:00:34.667
I think Squishies are trending
because the world we live in

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.500
just keeps on getting
more and more stressful.

00:00:40.354 --> 00:00:44.378
- I see where they get the
name from now, oh this is fun.

00:00:44.378 --> 00:00:46.961
(upbeat music)

00:00:48.691 --> 00:00:52.302
- This feels like a stress
ball but even squishier.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:54.023
- They're so squishy.

00:00:54.023 --> 00:00:56.281
- And they're super soft.

00:00:56.281 --> 00:00:58.076
- These are like dog toys for adults.

00:00:58.076 --> 00:01:00.482
- I don't actively play with
any toys still as an adult.

00:01:00.482 --> 00:01:01.440
- Can I have all of them?

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.345
- I really like these way
more than I thought I would.

00:01:04.345 --> 00:01:05.192
- Ohh they smell good.

00:01:05.192 --> 00:01:06.693
- I feel like if I choose one

00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:08.468
then the other squishies are gonna be sad

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.448
that I didn't choose them.

00:01:09.448 --> 00:01:10.686
- They're all staring at me.

00:01:10.686 --> 00:01:11.519
Look.

00:01:11.519 --> 00:01:12.848
Do you see this right now

00:01:12.848 --> 00:01:15.657
- (gasps) look how (laughs).

00:01:15.657 --> 00:01:17.095
- I'm gonna take this with me for a week,

00:01:17.095 --> 00:01:18.811
just hang out with it,
play around with it,

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.459
and kinda see how it affects me.

00:01:20.459 --> 00:01:22.885
- I'm pretty sure I will
get into fights with kids

00:01:22.885 --> 00:01:26.476
who will try to grab this from
me and that's not happening.

00:01:26.476 --> 00:01:27.465
These are my toys.

00:01:27.465 --> 00:01:28.908
- I'm a very stressed person,

00:01:28.908 --> 00:01:31.690
so I feel like they'll be
in handy when I'm stressed.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.905
- Am I suppose to like
squeeze it when I'm upset.

00:01:33.905 --> 00:01:36.406
(cries)

00:01:36.406 --> 00:01:38.023
- I think I'm already addicted (shrieks).

00:01:38.023 --> 00:01:39.338
- I might talk to them.

00:01:39.338 --> 00:01:41.175
- It's been less than an hour

00:01:41.175 --> 00:01:43.995
and I'm already starting to destroy it.

00:01:43.995 --> 00:01:45.155
But it's stress relief.

00:01:45.155 --> 00:01:49.301
- A man walking on the
road squishing a lemon,

00:01:49.301 --> 00:01:50.454
that's kind of a weird look.

00:01:50.454 --> 00:01:52.785
(truck horn)

00:01:52.785 --> 00:01:54.659
However, I'm enjoying it.

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:58.826
- I've had them for a couple
days now and they still smell

00:02:00.162 --> 00:02:01.561
frikkin delicious.

00:02:01.561 --> 00:02:03.469
- Oh my gosh, smells like vanilla wafers.

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:06.174
- This smells like a marshmallow,
this smells like plastic.

00:02:06.174 --> 00:02:07.007
- This smells good so.

00:02:07.007 --> 00:02:10.835
- I like how long it takes to
go back to it's original form.

00:02:10.835 --> 00:02:13.690
- [Girl] Squish, it looks sad.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.171
- He's about to be happy in a second.

00:02:15.171 --> 00:02:19.770
- I feel kind of wrong for
squishing this cute creature,

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.941
it's so cute, lemmi smash it.

00:02:22.941 --> 00:02:24.557
- It's really kind of grown on me

00:02:24.557 --> 00:02:26.500
and I still find myself subconsciously

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.223
squeezing it throughout the day

00:02:28.223 --> 00:02:29.702
or like fiddling around with it.

00:02:29.702 --> 00:02:33.869
I put it on my desk
just (knocking) mash it.

00:02:34.976 --> 00:02:37.117
- I'm the type of person
that fidgets a lot

00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:41.666
and I'm constantly biting on
my sweater and tapping my foot.

00:02:41.666 --> 00:02:43.470
Little Dugong over here
has helped me a lot

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.970
with my fidgeting.

00:02:46.186 --> 00:02:48.847
(speaks in foreign language)

00:02:48.847 --> 00:02:50.050
- We're about to take off.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:53.398
Usually this is when I
squeeze my husband's hand

00:02:53.398 --> 00:02:55.344
because I do freak out

00:02:55.344 --> 00:02:58.677
but these is gonna have to do this time.

00:03:00.321 --> 00:03:02.238
- Squish Squish Squish.

00:03:04.336 --> 00:03:06.858
- I did have a co-worker just
try to steal them from me,

00:03:06.858 --> 00:03:08.061
not good.

00:03:08.061 --> 00:03:10.474
- I feel so relaxed right now.

00:03:10.474 --> 00:03:13.440
- [Woman] No I need it back, I like it.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.035
I wanna go lay down with it.

00:03:15.035 --> 00:03:15.958
- [Woman] No.

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:17.834
- When I saw everyone
in the office had them,

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:21.084
I wanted one really bad so I stole one.

00:03:23.296 --> 00:03:27.129
- I forgot my daisy and
my feredigo right here

00:03:28.742 --> 00:03:30.153
in this studio.

00:03:30.153 --> 00:03:33.301
I didn't think it was
going to affect me so much.

00:03:33.301 --> 00:03:37.898
Oh my God I miss them so
frieking much, I really did.

00:03:37.898 --> 00:03:39.557
- I'm at the airport,
I had a minor freakout

00:03:39.557 --> 00:03:42.959
because I thought I left it
at home and I went to grab it

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:45.307
and my heart stopped

00:03:45.307 --> 00:03:47.140
cause I didn't think I
had it in my back pack.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.339
I have become squishy reliant.

00:03:49.339 --> 00:03:50.298
- I have an addiction.

00:03:50.298 --> 00:03:52.373
- They're not really a
stress reliever for me,

00:03:52.373 --> 00:03:56.270
they're more of my friends
and they keep me company.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:59.270
I think some people are scared of me now.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:02.062
- I've definitely noticed
that I've grown closer to it.

00:04:02.062 --> 00:04:05.901
- I have to throw it away
cause I have destroyed

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.334
what I once loved.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:09.775
So I literally squished it all weekend

00:04:09.775 --> 00:04:11.885
while I was laying in bed sick.

00:04:11.885 --> 00:04:15.303
I really love it and I'm
still holding and to it.

00:04:15.303 --> 00:04:19.162
- These really brought out a side of me

00:04:19.162 --> 00:04:21.303
that I did not expect to have.

00:04:21.303 --> 00:04:24.377
- I was kinda surprised
that I was so emotionally

00:04:24.377 --> 00:04:25.694
and physically attached to it.

00:04:25.694 --> 00:04:28.157
- They are my best friend's now.

00:04:28.157 --> 00:04:29.011
- I feel like it was a place

00:04:29.011 --> 00:04:31.690
to channel anxiety subconsciously.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.103
- It's been a really great stress reliever

00:04:33.103 --> 00:04:33.936
for me I would say.

00:04:33.936 --> 00:04:35.391
- Not a fan of flying.

00:04:35.391 --> 00:04:38.174
If anything happens at least I'm gonna die

00:04:38.174 --> 00:04:39.835
squeezing my squishies.

00:04:39.835 --> 00:04:43.643
- It felt really therapeutic actually.

00:04:43.643 --> 00:04:46.103
- I think its just having
something to do with my hands

00:04:46.103 --> 00:04:47.764
while I'm focused on that activity.

00:04:47.764 --> 00:04:48.661
- It looks like my dog chewed it

00:04:48.661 --> 00:04:50.193
but it was just me.

00:04:50.193 --> 00:04:52.909
Maybe I'm more stressed
out than I think that I am.

00:04:52.909 --> 00:04:54.393
- I feel like maybe what I learned

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:56.443
is that toys aren't just for kids.

00:04:56.443 --> 00:04:58.684
You play with toys and it can
take your mind off things.

00:04:58.684 --> 00:05:01.428
- I also learn that I
love to squish things.

00:05:01.428 --> 00:05:05.413
- It was a major surprise
to realize that yes,

00:05:05.413 --> 00:05:08.555
they become apart of me, it's
almost like an extension.

00:05:08.555 --> 00:05:10.029
- This is definitely staying on my desk.

00:05:10.029 --> 00:05:12.672
- You can pry my squishy
outta my cold dead hands.

00:05:12.672 --> 00:05:13.862
- [Woman] You can keep them.

00:05:13.862 --> 00:05:14.695
- Yes!

00:05:17.061 --> 00:05:19.644
There's no way you were
taking these from me anyways.

00:05:19.644 --> 00:05:23.420
- I wish everybody could
feel how squishy this is.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.423
Just like imagine.

00:05:25.423 --> 00:05:28.006
(upbeat music)

